{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared minute-interval vectors for the TimePicker's minute segment.",
    "Read by coui_core (CoreMinuteInterval), coui_flutter and coui_web (the",
    "TimePicker) — a change to where a typed minute lands, or to where an",
    "arrow key steps, fails on every platform at once.",
    "",
    "Derived by enumerating the multiples of each interval (not with the",
    "closed-form arithmetic the Dart implementation uses).",
    "",
    "The rules the tables state:",
    "- A minute past :59 is clamped to :59 first (the segment has always",
    "  clamped), then snapped.",
    "- snap: the nearest multiple of the interval, a tie going to the later",
    "  one (round half up). :60 is a candidate and wraps to :00; the hour is",
    "  never touched, so :53 at a 15-minute interval is :00 of the SAME hour.",
    "- up: the next multiple strictly after the minute, wrapping past the",
    "  last multiple to :00 without carrying into the hour.",
    "- down: the previous multiple strictly before the minute, wrapping",
    "  below :00 to the last multiple, again without borrowing from the",
    "  hour.",
    "- A minute that is already a multiple snaps to itself, so snapping is",
    "  idempotent.",
    "",
    "Each table is indexed by the minute 0..59: tables[interval][minute]."
  ],
